 without systemd (like this workspace), start Docker with:\n\n```bash\n# Start Docker daemon in the background\nsudo dockerd > /tmp/docker.log 2>&1 &\n\n# Wait for Docker to initialize\nsleep 5\n```\n\n## Verifying Docker Installation\n\nTo verify Docker is working correctly, run the hello-world container:\n\n```bash\nsudo docker run hello-world\n```\n</EXTRA_INFO>'}], 'role': 'user'}, {'content': [], 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_lucoWxFN7zNcljjSLurQkhSW', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'execute_bash', 'arguments': '{"command":"sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y docker.io"}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "Get:1 http://deb.debian.org/debian bookworm InRelease [151 kB]\nGet:2 http://deb.debian.org/debian bookworm-updates InRelease [55.4 kB]\nGet:3 http://deb.debian.org/debian-security bookworm-security InRelease [48.0 kB]\nGet:4 http://deb.debian.org/debian bookworm/main amd64 Packages [8793 kB]\nGet:5 http://deb.debian.org/debian bookworm-updates/main amd64 Packages [756 B]\nGet:6 http://deb.debian.org/debian-security bookworm-security/main amd64 Packages [272 kB]\nFetched 9320 kB in 1s (12.6 MB/s)\nReading package lists... Done\nReading package lists... Done\nBuilding dependency tree... Done\nReading state information... Done\nThe following additional packages will be installed:\n  apparmor cgroupfs-mount containerd criu dbus dbus-bin dbus-daemon dbus-session-bus-common dbus-system-bus-common dbus-user-session dmsetup gettext-base iproute2 iptables libapparmor1 libargon2-1 libatm1 libbpf1 libcap2-bin libcryptsetup12 libdevmapper1.02.1 libfdisk1 libintl-perl libintl-xs-perl libip4tc2 libip6tc2 libjson-c5 libkmod2 libmnl0 libmodule-find-perl libnet1 libnetfilter-conntrack3 libnfnetlink0 libnftables1 libnftnl11 libnl-3-200 libnss-systemd libpam-cap libpam-systemd libproc-processtable-perl libprotobuf-c1 libprotobuf32 libsort-naturally-perl libsystemd-shared libterm-readkey-perl libxtables12 needrestart nftables pyt